    "source_path": "<QPoints>/validation_records/reference_l1d_restore_100k/snapshot_0/INTENT.txt",
    "staged_path": "INTENT.txt",
    "text": "Run the committed timing-Ruby L1D restore path for `100000` instructions on the\n`l1d_frontend_mix` lineage and preserve both the reference outcome and a traced\nexplanation for the remaining L1D misses.\n\nPurpose:\n- confirm that L1D warm restore is active in gem5 with `LRURP`\n- capture a stable reference run for the restored `snapshot_0`\n- explain why `L1Dcache.m_demand_misses` remains non-zero after restoration\n\nReference status:\n- lifecycle state: `reference`\n- retention policy: `keep`\n- protected artifacts include the reference run stats/config/logs and the traced\n  miss-breakdown analysis bundle\n\nAcceptance criteria:\n1. the 8-way L1D restore run completes successfully\n2. `system.ruby.l1_cntrl0.L1Dcache.m_checkpoint_load_total > 0`\n3. `system.ruby.l1_cntrl0.L1Dcache.m_demand_hits > 0`\n4. the traced 2-set diagnostic run completes successfully and produces a data trace\n\nWhat this package validates:\n- the committed L1D restore path is active and materially useful\n- the benchmark's main 32 KiB data array is restored into the checkpointed L1D state\n- most remaining L1D misses are not from that main array, but from non-array runtime traffic\n"
  },
